  clock: 3  # 624e
  nonce: 624e  # 624e
  message: "CORRECTION to the cross-link note from WI-falum (2026-06-09): the suggested shared 'single-line TOML span unparseable' substrate does NOT apply to this item. Verified in code: this stable_id is produced by make_dependency_stable_id(language, name) = sha256('dependency:{language}:{name}')[:16] (analyze/base.py:591-598), which never touches the span — the cross-manifest collapse is purely hash-input-too-coarse (omits the declaring manifest path), squarely in the INV-tazaj family this item is parented under. WI-falum's collapse is a separate fingerprint-producer / tree-sitter span-parse defect on the same surface. The not_duplicate_of link is valid as RELATED_BUT_DISTINCT (same toml dependency-node surface) but the two have distinct root causes and will not resolve together."  # 624e
